---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site, href } from "../data/site";
---
<Base title="About" description="What the orchestra is, the crops and decisions it serves, and the two rules that make its results safe to act on." path="/about">
  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="kicker">About</p>
      <h1>An orchestra of packages for decisions based on cause and effect</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lead">Scientific analysis increasingly feeds a fitted model straight into an automated
        decision, and the risk is easy to miss: a model that fits an outcome well can still rest on an
        association that is driven by some third factor, or that nobody has checked, and a pipeline that
        simply tunes a model and then optimises against it will act on that association.</p>
      <p class="mt-2">The orchestra's answer is to build from small packages, each doing one job, held to
        firm rules. Every package writes its results in the same versioned record, the manifest, and an
        engine runs the analysis plan, checking at each step that the result passed on is the kind the next
        step expects. Two rules carry the weight. <strong>Declining to answer</strong>: the system gives no
        recommendation when the evidence is too thin to detect the effect, when the different methods applied
        to the same question disagree, or when an input has not been checked, and it records why. And
        <strong>the independent-check rule</strong>: every fact about an outside source (a service, a
        dataset's columns, a constant, a citation) is checked against a reference the orchestra did not
        produce itself, and a fact that has not been checked is refused rather than acted on.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-3">Domain</h2>
      <p class="mt-1">{site.domain}. Every method must be shown working on a real grain-production
        decision; a method that cannot be is set aside, not pursued. All data used are data that can be
        published (public agricultural trial datasets and crop simulators); no restricted field data
        enters any package.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-3">How this site was checked</h2>
      <p class="mt-1">Every package name, capability, interface between packages, count and number on
        this site was checked against the orchestra's own records before it was shown; where a fact could
        not be checked, it was left out or marked as open. The newer outside tools the site describes were
        checked against their official sources. The site is held to the same standard as the orchestra's
        science.</p>

      <p class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={href("/members")}>The packages</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={href("/")}>Home</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
